In this code, we initialize an array `fib` with the first two elements of the Fibonacci series. Then iteratively, we add the previous two numbers to compute the next Fibonacci number. This way, we compute all Fibonacci numbers till `n`. Finally, we return the `n-th` Fibonacci number. 

This algorithm runs in O(n) time and uses O(n) space. However, note that we can optimize it to use O(1) space by only storing the last two Fibonacci numbers because these are the only ones used to calculate the next Fibonacci number. 

