You are given a dictionary that contains N correctly-spelled English words.  For every presentation word that is suspected to be wrong you have to output the unique word of the dictionary that matches it within at most one single-letter error.

A presentation word is considered to match a dictionary word if one of the following holds
1. it is exactly the same word;
2. it can become the dictionary word by changing exactly one letter (substitution);
3. it can become the dictionary word by inserting exactly one letter (the presentation word is missing one letter);
4. it can become the dictionary word by deleting exactly one letter (the presentation word has one extra letter).

It is guaranteed that for every presentation word there exists exactly one dictionary word that satisfies the above rules.

Input
The first line contains an integer T – the number of test cases.
For each test case:
• a line with two integers N and Q (1 ≤ N,Q ≤ 200) – the number of dictionary words and the number of presentation words;
• N lines follow, each containing one dictionary word composed of lowercase letters (length 1 … 100);
• Q lines follow, each containing one presentation word (also lowercase, length 1 … 100).

Output
For every presentation word print, on its own line, the corresponding dictionary word.

All input is read from standard input and all output must be written to standard output.

import sys

ALPHA = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'

def find_correct_word(word, dset):
    # exact match
    if word in dset:
        return word

    L = len(word)
    # substitution (same length)
    for i in range(L):
        original = word[i]
        for ch in ALPHA:
            if ch == original:
                continue
            cand = word[:i] + ch + word[i+1:]
            if cand in dset:
                return cand

    # insertion (dictionary word longer by 1)
    for i in range(L + 1):
        for ch in ALPHA:
            cand = word[:i] + ch + word[i:]
            if cand in dset:
                return cand

    # deletion (dictionary word shorter by 1)
    for i in range(L):
        cand = word[:i] + word[i+1:]
        if cand in dset:
            return cand
    # per statement this will never be reached
    return None

def main():
    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()  # fast tokenisation
    it = iter(data)
    t = int(next(it))
    for _ in range(t):
        N = int(next(it)); Q = int(next(it))
        dset = {next(it) for _ in range(N)}
        for _ in range(Q):
            w = next(it)
            print(find_correct_word(w, dset))

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()

