    """Craft a function that caters a dictionary which includes the smallest index of an element which is not lesser than or equal to the preceding element, the index of the following greater element that can be swapped to ordering the sequence, and the total count of needed swaps. Return {'index': -1, 'swap_with': -1, 'total_swaps': 0} in case there is not any such element. The input list will exclude any duplicate elements.

    Examples:
    optimize_arrangement([5,3,4,1,2]) = {'index': 1, 'swap_with': 2, 'total_swaps': 1}
