In your JavaScript file (script.js), use the Fetch API to query your API.

```javascript
fetch('http://your_api_url')
    .then(response => {
        if (!response.ok) {
            throw new Error("HTTP error " + response.status);
        }
        return response.json();
    })
    .then(json => {
      document.getElementById('name').textContent = 'Name: ' + json.name;
      document.getElementById('age').textContent = 'Age: ' + json.age;
