public class Student {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    private Map<String, Integer> grades; // To manage multiple subjects and their respective grades.

    // Constructor
    public Student(String name, int age){
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
        this.grades = new HashMap<>();
    }

    // Setter & Getter methods for Name and Age.
    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }

    public void setAge(int age) {
        this.age = age;
    }

    // Methods for handling grades
    public void addGrade(String subject, int grade){
        if(grade < 0 || grade > 100){
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Grade must be between 0 and 100.");
        }
        this.grades.put(subject, grade);
    }

    public int getGrade(String subject){
        if(this.grades.containsKey(subject)){
            return this.grades.get(subject);
        }
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("No grade exists for the provided subject.");
    }

    // Method to calculate the grade point average (GPA)
    public double calculateGPA(){
        if(this.grades.isEmpty()){
            throw new IllegalStateException("No grades to calculate GPA.");
        }

        double sum = 0;
        for(int grade : this.grades.values()){
            sum += grade;
        }

        return sum / this.grades.size();
    }
}
```
In the refactored code, a `HashMap` is used to store the grades of multiple subjects for each student object. Please note that the `addGrade()` method throws an `IllegalArgumentException` if the grade is not between 0 and 100 and the `getGrade()` method throws an `IllegalArgumentException` if it is called with a subject that the student has no grade for. The `calculateGPA()` method throws an `IllegalStateException` if it is called for a student that has no grades yet. These exceptions are meant to illustrate the concept of error handling and might be adjusted according to the actual needs of your application.

