PHP does not have built-in packages to handle advanced mathematical operations like NumPy in Python. However, below is an equivalent PHP code that calculates both the average, median, and frequency of numbers in a list.

```php
function rolling_avg_median_and_frequency($numbers) {
    $stats = [];
    $freq_dict = [];
    foreach ($numbers as $i => $num) {
        // Update frequency dictionary
        if (array_key_exists($num, $freq_dict)) {
            $freq_dict[$num]++;
        } else {
            $freq_dict[$num] = 1;
        }

        // Calculate rolling average and median
        $avg = array_sum(array_slice($numbers, 0, $i+1)) / count(array_slice($numbers, 0, $i+1));

        $middle_value = floor(count(array_slice($numbers, 0, $i+1)) / 2);
        $sliced_array = array_slice($numbers, 0, $i+1);
        sort($sliced_array);

        if(count($sliced_array) % 2) {
            $median = $sliced_array[$middle_value];
        } else {
            $low = $sliced_array[$middle_value];
            $high = $sliced_array[$middle_value + 1];
            $median = (($low + $high) / 2);
        }

        $stats[] = [$avg, $median];
    }

    return [$stats, $freq_dict];
}
```
