This JavaScript code attaches a click event listener to the button with ID 'change'. It captures the text in the 'content' element, splits it into an array of words, transforms each word based on its position—odd-indexed words are wrapped in italic tags `<i>` and `<\i>`, while even-indexed words are enwrapped by bold tags `<b>` and `<\b>`. It then joins the transformed words back into a string with spaces in between and replaces the original text in the 'content' element with the result. 

Please note that the first word is considered as 0 index and is made bold. If you want the first word to be italic and second to be bold, you may subtract 1 from index in the if condition, like this: `if ((index - 1) % 2 === 0)`.

