4. Checked whether the digit is prime or composite by a switch statement. If it is prime, we incremented the `primeCount`, and if it is composite, we incremented the `compositeCount`.
5. Finally, returned a tuple (in Go it is a two-element array) containing the count of prime and composite digits.

