In this code, `result.main` will contain the cumulative total of all elements in the main array, and `result.nested[index]` will contain the cumulative total of all elements in the nested array at depth `index`. For example, with `array` being `[1, 2, [3, 4]]`, the output will be `{ main: 3, nested: [7] }`, meaning the cumulative total of the main array is 3, and the cumulative total of the first nested array is 7.

