Here is a JavaScript function that calculates the roots of a quadratic equation:

```javascript
function quadraticRoots(a, b, c) {
    // calculate the determinant b^2 - 4ac
    var determinant = b*b - 4*a*c;
    var sqrtval = Math.sqrt(Math.abs(determinant));  
    // check if determinant is positive, negative or zero
    if (determinant > 0) {
        // roots are real and different 
        return [ (-b + sqrtval) / (2*a) , (-b - sqrtval) / (2*a) ];
    } 
    else if (determinant == 0) {
        // roots are real and the same
        return [-b / (2*a)];
    } 
    else {
        // roots are complex (not real)
        var realPart = -b/(2*a);
        var imaginaryPart = sqrtval/(2*a);
        return [ `${realPart} + ${imaginaryPart}i` , `${realPart} - ${imaginaryPart}i` ];
    }
}
```

You can test this function with a quadratic equation:

```javascript
