var y = 'World';
var result = interchangeData(x, y);
console.log('Interchanged values:', 'x =', result.a, '& y =', result.b);
```

Please note that JavaScript passes parameters by value (for primitive types) and by reference (for objects). Therefore, if you interchange the values of two variables inside a function, those changes will not be reflected outside of that function. In the function interchangeData, a and b are merely copies of x and y, so swapping a and b does not affect x and y.

