This program first combines the two given arrays into one and then sorts the combined array in descending order. Quicksort is a divide-and-conquer sorting algorithm which works by selecting a 'pivot' element from the array and partitioning the other elements into two sub-arrays, according to whether they are less than or greater than the pivot. The sub-arrays are then recursively sorted.

