Given an array `A` of `n` distinct integers, the algorithm finds the first pair of elements whose sum is equal to a given target value `T`. The algorithm is as follows:

1. Use two pointers: one starting at the beginning (`i = 0`) and one at the end (`j = n-1`) of the array.
2. Move the pointers towards each other until the sum of the elements at these pointers equals `T` or the pointers cross each other.

Formally, the pseudocode is:
```
i = 0
j = n - 1
while (i < j) {
    if (A[i] + A[j] == T) {
        return (i, j)
    } else if (A[i] + A[j] < T) {
        i = i + 1
    } else {
        j = j - 1
    }
}
return (-1, -1) // No pair found
