When determining the index of the object, any non-object elements should be disregarded.

Additionally, you are required to test and rectify the provided piece of faulty code, which was designed to perform as described above but contains some bugs.

```javascript
function sumMultiplication(obj, index = 0) {
    let sum = 0;
    if (!obj || typeof obj !== &#39;object&#39;) {
        return 0;
    }
    for (let key in obj) {
        if (obj.hasOwnProperty(key)) {
            let value = obj[key];
            if (typeof value === &#39;object&#39;) {
                sum += sumMultiplication(value, index + 1);
            } else {
                sum += value * index;
            }
