- Added `Array.isArray(value)` in the condition to check whether value is an array. This is because in JavaScript arrays are also considered objects.
- `try...catch` block introduced to handle potential exceptions and errors.
- Added an error-handling condition to throw an error when the value is not a number. Position of this condition is crucial as we want to allow objects and arrays for nested traversal, but disallow any non-number primitive types or `null`. If the value is not an object, an array, or a number, then an error will be thrown.
