In this code, `mean_recursive` and `std_dev_recursive` are helper functions to compute the mean and standard deviation of an array respectively. 

The function `normalize_recursive` normalized the given array by subtracting the mean and dividing by the standard deviation.

The function `denormalize` restores the normalized array back to its original form, by multiplying with the standard deviation and adding the mean.

Note that all computations in these functions are done using built-in python functionality, no external packages are used. Also, a TypeError is handled when the input is not an array. 

