You can accomplish this in Java by creating a new 2D array and copying the values from the original array into the new one in a rotated manner, iterating over columns of original array from first to last and rows of the original array from last to first. Here's a possible Java code to do this.

```java
public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[][] data = {{1, 2}, {3, 4}};

        int[][] rotatedData = rotate90Clockwise(data);

        // Printing the rotated array
        for (int i = 0; i < rotatedData.length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < rotatedData[i].length; j++) {
                System.out.print(rotatedData[i][j] + " ");
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }

    static int[][] rotate90Clockwise(int[][] data) {

        int N = data.length;
        int[][] rotatedData = new int[N][N];

        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) 
            for (int j = 0; j < N; j++) 
                rotatedData[j][N-1-i] = data[i][j]; 

        return rotatedData;
    }
}
```
