Please note that this "(COLOR ##)" command is specific to windows cmd and may not work in other types of terminal or command line interfaces. For instance, in a Unix-like system's terminal, you'll have to use an escape sequence to change the color.

For more universal support, you should not rely on changing the colors of the command line, but instead use a more sophisticated library for console output that supports colors, like ncurses for Unix-like systems or the Windows console API for Windows.

Remember that this will change the color for the whole command prompt window, not just for the output of your program.

It's also considered bad practice to depend on specific system commands in your programs. This will make your program less portable, as it will only work on systems where the color command is available. Therefore, use such commands sparingly or include alternatives for different platforms to make your program more portable.

