Additionally, the class should be able to handle incorrect inputs gracefully without causing intractable errors. Also, ensure the solution has optimized time complexity and resource utilization.

Here is the basic structure of the class:
``` java
class QuadraticSum {
    int start, end;

    // Constructor
    QuadraticSum(int k, int n) {
        start = k;
        end = n;
    }

    // Calculate method
    int calculate() {
        int total = 0;
        for (int i = start; i <= end; i++) {
            if (i % 2 == 0) {
                total += i * i;
            }
        }
        return total;
    }
