This `defaultText` directive that I've created accepts a `defaultText` attribute, and if the model value is empty or undefined, it will use the value of this attribute as default content. It pushes a function into the `ngModelCtrl.$formatters` array. This function is used to control how the value is displayed to the user in the input control.

